<%# SafeFile JP blog article (primary_locale = "ja").
    Separate from the Korean layout on purpose: that one is a conversion page
    built around loss framing (error mockup, loss box, stats cards, two CTAs)
    with its copy hardcoded in Korean. The JP strategy forbids most of it —
    v3.1 §3-1 rules out fear appeals, first-person brand voice and 「あなた」 —
    so reusing the shell would mean suppressing two thirds of it with
    conditionals and leaving Korean strings in a Japanese document.

    `url_locale` decides which body is shown (ja, or en on /en/blog/:slug when
    body_en exists). The page never reads I18n.locale: the content has to be a
    property of the URL, which is the bug this app already shipped once.
%>
<% showing_en = url_locale.to_sym == :en && post.body_en.present? %>
<%# ?via=blog&ep=NN, not ?utm_* (S10) — blocking extensions strip the latter
    before the request is made, so these in-article CTA clicks were arriving
    with no recorded source. Named `utm` still because the variable is used
    below in several places and the rename buys nothing; the VALUE is the new
    form. JpWeeklyKpi counts `via=blog` in P16's DENOMINATOR only, same as it
    did for utm_source=blog — an in-article link is internal navigation, and
    counting it as social would make the metric rise as the blog grows. %>
<% utm = "via=blog&ep=ep#{format('%02d', post.content_ep.to_i)}" %>
<% landing = post.package["landing_path"].presence || "/safe/jp/nyusatsu/" %>

<article class="jp-article" lang="<%= showing_en ? "en" : "ja" %>">
  <header class="jp-article-head">
    <% if post.package["intent"].present? %>
      <div class="jp-article-tag"><%= post.package["intent"] %></div>
    <% end %>
    <h1><%= post.title(url_locale) %></h1>
    <% if post.subtitle(url_locale).present? %>
      <p class="jp-article-sub"><%= post.subtitle(url_locale) %></p>
    <% end %>
    <div class="jp-article-meta">
      <time datetime="<%= post.published_at&.iso8601 %>">
        <%= post.published_at&.in_time_zone("Asia/Tokyo")&.strftime(showing_en ? "%B %-d, %Y" : "%Y年%-m月%-d日") %>
      </time>
    </div>
  </header>

  <% if post.hero_image.attached? %>
    <figure class="jp-article-hero">
      <%= image_tag post.hero_image, alt: post.title(url_locale), loading: "eager" %>
    </figure>
  <% end %>

  <div class="jp-article-body">
    <%= post.body(url_locale).to_s.html_safe %>
  </div>

  <%# FAQ is rendered as real content, not only as JSON-LD. Structured data that
      describes a section the document does not contain is a false claim about
      the page — so the markup and the JSON-LD in show.html.erb read the same
      list, and both are absent together. %>
  <% if faq.present? %>
    <section class="jp-article-faq">
      <h2><%= showing_en ? "Frequently asked questions" : "よくある質問" %></h2>
      <% faq.each do |entry| %>
        <div class="jp-faq-item">
          <h3><%= entry["q"] %></h3>
          <p><%= entry["a"] %></p>
        </div>
      <% end %>
    </section>
  <% end %>

  <aside class="jp-article-cta">
    <a href="<%= landing %>?<%= utm %>" class="jp-cta-link">
      <%= showing_en ? "Try it in the browser" : "ブラウザだけで試す" %>
    </a>
    <p class="jp-cta-note">
      <%= showing_en ?
            "Files are processed inside the browser and are not sent to a server. No sign-up." :
            "ファイルはブラウザの中だけで処理され、サーバーには送信されません。登録も不要です。" %>
    </p>
  </aside>

  <nav class="jp-article-nav">
    <a href="/ja/blog"><%= showing_en ? "← All posts" : "← 記事一覧" %></a>
  </nav>
</article>
